OL,3,ALib Dems vow to end 'computer says no'
OL,4,Aeconomy to boost growth
OL,5,
OL,6,FLiberal Democrat deputy leader Daisy
OL,7,FCooper has warned the UK's economic
OL,8,Fgrowth is being held back by a
OL,9,F"computer says no" approach.
OL,11,FShe unveiled a 30-page growth plan
OL,12,Faimed at removing barriers to business
OL,13,Fas part of her speech to the Lib Dem
OL,14,Fconference in Brighton.
OL,16,FCooper, who is also the party's
OL,17,FTreasury spokesperson, said too many
OL,18,Fideas, start-ups and research started
OL,19,Fin Britain but ended up being taken
OL,20,Foverseas.
OL,23,APub: 20-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
